Here is the commit message:
OOZIE-1989 NPE during a rerun with forks (rkanter)

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the `compare` method in the `LiteWorkflowInstance` class attempting to compare two `Date` objects that were initialized to `null`. When either `date1` or `date2` was `null`, it led to a NullPointerException during the comparison, particularly in scenarios involving reruns with forks where the action end times might not have been set, resulting in the absence of values for the nodes being compared.

Here is the patch:

         @Override
         public int compare(String node1, String node2) {
-            Date date1 = FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE;
-            Date date2 = FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE;
+            Date date1 = null;
+            Date date2 = null;
             NodeInstance node1Instance = executionPaths.get(node1);
             if (node1Instance != null) {
                 date1 = this.actionEndTimes.get(node1Instance.nodeName);
             }
             NodeInstance node2Instance = executionPaths.get(node2);
             if (node2Instance != null) {
                 date2 = this.actionEndTimes.get(node2Instance.nodeName);
             }
+            date1 = (date1 == null) ? FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE : date1;
+            date2 = (date2 == null) ? FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE : date2;
             return date1.compareTo(date2);
         }



